bility, communication.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Strengths: conscientious (reliability), stress handling, weather assessment (technical), computer skills. Concerns: weak memory for numbers (attention), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication). No info on decision quality.\n\nC: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Strengths: decision quality, calm under pressure, technical competence. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric (cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). Good.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, has a hot temper. Strengths: adaptability to unexpected, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: know-it-all (cooperation), hot temper (stress resilience, crew cooperation). No info on technical competence.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? C has strong decision, calm, technical, but communication issues and egocentric. B has reliability and stress but nasty remarks. D has responsibility but hot temper. A has anticipation and leadership but show-off and not open.\n\nProbably C seems strongest on core pilot criteria (decision, calm, technical). Communication is important but maybe can be mitigated. Egocentric also concerning. B's nasty remarks severe for crew cooperation. D's hot temper also severe. A's not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference facts: \"makes correct decisions quickly\" and \"keeps calm in a crisis\" as strengths, and note concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\" and \"regarded as egocentric\". Explain why still best.\n\nProceed."}
